From 867020fb463eedb5a04d05dc769081c19d63fbf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolas Gauder <nikolas.gauder@tum.de>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:42:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] util/mkerr.pl: only replace the .ec suffix when naming the
 state file

When no state file is configured, mkerr.pl derives it from the config
file path with s/.ec/.txt/.  The unescaped, unanchored pattern replaces
the first occurrence of any character followed by "ec" anywhere
in the path.  Since the error headers are generated at build time,
mkerr.pl runs with -conf $(SRCDIR)/crypto/err/openssl.ec,
so an out-of-tree build whose relative source path contains a name
such as "projects" fails:

    Can't open ../pro.txtts/openssl/crypto/err/openssl.ec

Anchor the pattern to the ".ec" suffix.

Fixes: 52df25cf2e65 "make error tables const and separate header file"
Complements: 7a3fa58d9da7 "Generate the error headers and tables at build time"
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Merge-date: Tue Oct 27 18:11:11 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33389
(cherry picked from commit 93d5616734b9a11bc180cda496222f658ccdbd29)
---
 util/mkerr.pl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/util/mkerr.pl b/util/mkerr.pl
index e2479e727b74..c4d6b331376a 100755
--- a/util/mkerr.pl
+++ b/util/mkerr.pl
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ close IN;
 
 if ( ! $statefile ) {
     $statefile = $config;
-    $statefile =~ s/.ec/.txt/;
+    $statefile =~ s/\.ec$/.txt/;
 }
 
 # The statefile has all the previous assignments.
